&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive is a dynamic agency and creative collective operating at the speed of culture. We’re a collective of deep thinkers, creative makers, cultural connoisseurs, and executional aces. We create meaningful engagements between brands and their audiences, cultivating relationships that drive tangible results for our clients. And we do it with sharp strategy and powerful creative executed across all the media and touch-points key to our targets’ lives.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;As pioneers in the area of content, digital engagement, and innovative experiential programs, and award winners for work in TV, event, digital and social, Motive has created a culture where every individual is given an opportunity to stretch and flex their creative and executional muscles daily. We are a team of hard-working, fast-moving, energetic, passionate, driven, straight-talking creative thinkers. We like being challenged and we love the collaboration necessary to overcome the challenges and succeed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If this sounds like a place you would thrive, let’s see if we can make something happen.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt; at Motive, you play a key role in the day-to-day execution of client work. You are the connective tissue between the client and our internal teams—responsible for driving projects forward, supporting strategic thinking, and ensuring work is delivered on time, on brief, and within budget.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a foundational role on the account team, offering exposure to a broad range of work including traditional, experiential, digital, promotional and media. You’ll collaborate with creative, strategy, brand experience and production, as well as other departments while continuing to grow your skills as a marketer, project manager, and client partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the account team in managing daily client communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships based on trust, responsiveness, and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help translate client needs into agency action—balancing what’s best for the client and what’s best for the work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project &amp;amp; Process Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own specific projects and workstreams, from brief through delivery or activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear, actionable briefs for internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track timelines, deliverables, budgets and client feedback to keep projects moving smoothly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively flag and escalate risks or delays and help problem-solve with your team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Stewardship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate confidence with the financial process, leading with proactivity and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process client invoices, manage PO and job number requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized files and documentation for all assigned projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support budget tracking and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin SOW development training, and learn how to build and manage project-level SOWs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on creation of estimates with internal studios based on program needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creative Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with creative, strategy, brand experience, and other departments to bring ideas to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in brainstorms and concept reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help ensure the final output meets both the creative vision and client expectations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrated Marketing Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support a wide range of campaign types— experiential, advertising, retail and promotional, social and digital.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn to navigate the nuances of each discipline and how they work together as part of integrated brand experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able and willing to travel to client events and activations in a working capacity, leading or supporting depending on the program.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Team Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help coordinate and support cross-functional team efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized documentation and status updates across projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed on your clients’ industries and competitors to contribute meaningfully to discussions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success in This Role Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re seen as reliable, organized, and solutions-oriented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal teams trust you to keep projects on track and informed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clients view you as a capable, responsive partner who understands their business, listens to them and knows how to action provided direction and feedback appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are actively learning and growing your skills in client service, creative development, and marketing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly, collaborate openly, and always aim to make the work—and the process—better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong foundational understanding of the sports landscape and how it works. From youth sports through professional leagues and organizations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Skills for the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in an integrated agency environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with experiential, retail and promotional marketing, as well as experience with digital and social.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and organizational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, team-first mindset and a drive to keep learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An instinct to figure things out, but know when to ask for input to keep things on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or activating brand partnerships across a range of properties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Motive is an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;equal opportunity employer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;! We believe that a diverse team makes us stronger and smarter.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Motive recruits, employs, trains, compensates and promotes regardless of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, veteran status, and other protected status as required by applicable law. We offer an inspiring working environment and great benefits, including employer-paid health, dental, vision, unlimited flex time off, 401k with annual match and more. The starting salary for this position is between $60k and $70k annually, based on experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Motive has a clear vision: to be a creative leader where a diverse mix of talented people want to come, to stay and do their best work. We know our company succeeds only through the hard work and dedication of our passionate and creative employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive is a dynamic agency and creative collective operating at the speed of culture. We’re a collective of deep thinkers, creative makers, cultural connoisseurs, and executional aces. We create meaningful engagements between brands and their audiences, cultivating relationships that drive tangible results for our clients. And we do it with sharp strategy and powerful creative executed across all the media and touch-points key to our targets’ lives.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As pioneers in the area of content, digital engagement, and innovative experiential programs, and award winners for work in TV, event, digital and social, Motive has created a culture where every individual is given an opportunity to stretch and flex their creative and executional muscles daily. We are a team of hard-working, fast-moving, energetic, passionate, driven, straight-talking creative thinkers. We like being challenged and we love the collaboration necessary to overcome the challenges and succeed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If this sounds like a place you would thrive, let’s see if we can make something happen.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ACCOUNT SUPERVISOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a hybrid position, meaning you&#39;re empowered to work from home and our local office location.&amp;nbsp; We currently require a minimum of 1 day of intentional collaboration work in the office per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At this time we are currently only interviewing candidates based in the Denver area.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As an Account Supervisor at Motive you’ll have the opportunity to manage the integrated day-to-day efforts with key client relationships and accounts. You’ll partner with clients to understand their business and work with internal teams to develop meaningful fully-integrated marketing campaigns that deliver results. On any given day you will write briefs, lead creative and partnership initiatives, manage communications, orchestrate an organized asset delivery plan, be responsible for budgets and timelines, collaborate with creative and other internal and external teams, while managing a variety of projects. You’ll be responsible for championing best-in-class work across traditional, retail, promotional, partnerships, experiential and more for some of the biggest brands in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage the day-to-day efforts with key clients, and the day-to-day internal project management flow for high-profile projects for major international brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Serve as key contact for day-to-day projects, managing communication and asset distribution, and serving as the central touch point for questions, strategic guidance and support for internal and client teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage a variety of work streams which could include TVC, social, events, retail / shopper, POS / POP,&amp;nbsp; digital, partnerships; including creation of timelines, workflows, and budgets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically advise clients and develop ideas and solutions that achieve business, marketing and engagement objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate client assignments into meaningful briefs for the creative teams and effectively balance dual expectations of clients and the agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a cross-studio team of art directors, copywriters, experiential leads, digital and social innovators, as well as and other client services teams to ideate and develop concepts for projects and accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-task and get the work done—on time, within project budgets and exceeding expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in big idea thinking sessions for the agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquire in-depth knowledge of, and be conversant in, client’s business, industry and competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster client relationships that run deep. Step into the role of your client&#39;s &quot;go to&quot; lead, managing proactive communications in an inspiring and professional manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively present strategic and creative platforms to internal and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 6 years of experience managing integrated (read: a combination of traditional, retail, shopper, digital / social partnerships and promotional) projects and accounts in a fast-paced advertising agency.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience managing several projects simultaneously.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Exemplary organizational skills: you&#39;re known for having your finger on the pulse and every detail locked-in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Powerhouse communications: you&#39;re clear, direct, proactive and kind. You can communicate up, down, and sideways if you have to - building trust, rapport, and relationships in the process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of owned social, with experience helping shape strategies that connect brand objectives, audience behaviors and platform opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;w4vq38&quot; data-start=&quot;849&quot; data-end=&quot;996&quot;&gt;Experience with bringing content to life -&amp;nbsp;leading the development and production of still and video assets from brief through final delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience crafting big idea briefs, and guiding creative concept and design work forward.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience creating and managing budgets and timelines for projects covering all of the above.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, and a knack for delivering excellent presentations and building relationships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A strong ‘self-starter’ mentality and sense of responsibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A passion for culture, creativity, and advertising.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience leading and coaching junior team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An excellent reputation for managing up.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A positive, upbeat attitude! We love what we do, and we love the people we work with - we want to build our team with like-minded folks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Motive is an&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;equal opportunity employer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;! We believe that a diverse team makes us stronger and smarter.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive recruits, employs, trains, compensates and promotes regardless of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, veteran status, and other protected status as required by applicable law. The starting salary for this position is between $80k and $110k annually, based on experience. We offer an inspiring working environment and great benefits, including low-cost health, dental, and vision plans; unlimited flexible paid time off, 401k with annual match, an employee stock ownership program and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive has a clear vision: to be a creative leader where a diverse mix of talented people want to come, stay, and do their best work. We know our company succeeds only through the hard work and dedication of our passionate and creative employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1 data-start=&quot;242&quot; data-end=&quot;299&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;244&quot; data-end=&quot;297&quot;&gt;Assistant Market Manager – Retail Direct Engagement Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;300&quot; data-end=&quot;553&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;300&quot; data-end=&quot;313&quot;&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Austin, TX (In-Market Role | Up to 40-mile radius from Austin, TX)&lt;br data-start=&quot;389&quot; data-end=&quot;392&quot;&gt;&lt;br data-start=&quot;460&quot; data-end=&quot;463&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for an energetic and hands-on Assistant Manager to play a pivotal role in a&amp;nbsp;multi-week retail engagement program. This position assists the Market Manager by contributing&amp;nbsp;to on-the-ground operations and supporting a team of Field Specialists to deliver effective&amp;nbsp;program activity in a highly regulated industry (tobacco/nicotine). The ideal candidate excels in&amp;nbsp;leadership, communication, and possesses a strong ability to motivate and guide teams in a&amp;nbsp;dynamic convenience store environment.&amp;nbsp;The Assistant Manager will serve as a daily operational leader, ensuring Field Specialists are&amp;nbsp;prepared, supported, and performing at their best. This includes conducting site visits, providing&amp;nbsp;real-time coaching, and addressing challenges as they arise to maintain program standards and&amp;nbsp;compliance. They will assist with training execution, performance monitoring, and quality&lt;br&gt;assurance, ensuring every activation meets brand and regulatory expectations. This role requires flexibility, strong organizational skills, and a proactive mindset to keep operations running smoothly across multiple locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Support and Reporting: Partner with the Market Manager to execute retail strategies and&amp;nbsp;provide comprehensive reports on field activities and performance metrics&lt;br&gt;● Retail Communication and Relations: Cultivate and sustain strong relationships with&amp;nbsp;retail partners to ensure smooth program operations, addressing and resolving issues&amp;nbsp;with professionalism.&lt;br&gt;● Leadership and Development: Guide and develop Field Specialists by providing&amp;nbsp;essential tools and knowledge. Assisting with regular training sessions and ongoing&amp;nbsp;support.&lt;br&gt;● Program Optimization: Collect and analyze on-site feedback to refine program tactics,&amp;nbsp;while implementing effective solutions to boost program efficiency.&lt;br&gt;● Inventory Oversight: Aide in distribution and tracking of program materials and assets,&amp;nbsp;ensuring timely communication of issues and escalation as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● 1-3 years of experience in field marketing, brand activation, retail engagement, or similar&amp;nbsp;roles.&lt;br&gt;● Proven supervisory experience with a strong focus on team development and coaching.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● Solid understanding of compliance requirements in regulated industries and the ability to enforce guidelines consistently.&lt;br&gt;● Highly organized with excellent problem-solving skills and meticulous attention to detail.&lt;br&gt;● Demonstrated ability to quickly learn and articulate detailed product information.&lt;br&gt;● Strong communication skills with a talent for building meaningful relationships.&lt;br&gt;● Availability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends as needed.&lt;br&gt;● Must be 25+ years of age with a valid driver&#39;s license and reliable transportation.&lt;br&gt;● In-market travel required up to a 40-mile radius.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We seek a leader who thrives on being actively involved in every facet of the retail program. The&amp;nbsp;ideal candidate will be deeply involved in day-to-day operations—mentoring a team of&amp;nbsp;specialists, ensuring compliance, and driving performance across every consumer and retailer&amp;nbsp;relationship built. Your hands-on approach and commitment to excellence will directly impact&amp;nbsp;program success.&lt;/p&gt;

