&lt;p&gt;● Solid understanding of compliance requirements in regulated industries and the ability to enforce guidelines consistently.&lt;br&gt;● Highly organized with excellent problem-solving skills and meticulous attention to detail.&lt;br&gt;● Demonstrated ability to quickly learn and articulate detailed product information.&lt;br&gt;● Strong communication skills with a talent for building meaningful relationships.&lt;br&gt;● Availability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends as needed.&lt;br&gt;● Must be 25+ years of age with a valid driver&#39;s license and reliable transportation.&lt;br&gt;● In-market travel required up to a 40-mile radius.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We seek a leader who thrives on being actively involved in every facet of the retail program. The&amp;nbsp;ideal candidate will be deeply involved in day-to-day operations—mentoring a team of&amp;nbsp;specialists, ensuring compliance, and driving performance across every consumer and retailer&amp;nbsp;relationship built. Your hands-on approach and commitment to excellence will directly impact&amp;nbsp;program success.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1 data-start=&quot;242&quot; data-end=&quot;299&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;244&quot; data-end=&quot;297&quot;&gt;Assistant Market Manager – Retail Direct Engagement Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;300&quot; data-end=&quot;553&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;300&quot; data-end=&quot;313&quot;&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Charlotte, NC (In-Market Role | Up to 40-mile radius from Oklahoma City, OK)&lt;br data-start=&quot;389&quot; data-end=&quot;392&quot;&gt;&lt;br data-start=&quot;460&quot; data-end=&quot;463&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for an energetic and hands-on Assistant Manager to play a pivotal role in a multi-week retail engagement program. This position assists the Market Manager by contributing to on-the-ground operations and supporting a team of Field Specialists to deliver effective program activity in a highly regulated industry (tobacco/nicotine). The ideal candidate excels in leadership, communication, and possesses a strong ability to motivate and guide teams in a dynamic convenience store environment. The Assistant Manager will serve as a daily operational leader, ensuring Field Specialists are prepared, supported, and performing at their best. This includes conducting site visits, providing real-time coaching, and addressing challenges as they arise to maintain program standards and compliance. They will assist with training execution, performance monitoring, and quality&amp;nbsp;assurance, ensuring every activation meets brand and regulatory expectations. This role requires flexibility, strong organizational skills, and a proactive mindset to keep operations running smoothly across multiple locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Support and Reporting: Partner with the Market Manager to execute retail strategies and&amp;nbsp;provide comprehensive reports on field activities and performance metrics&lt;br&gt;● Retail Communication and Relations: Cultivate and sustain strong relationships with&amp;nbsp;retail partners to ensure smooth program operations, addressing and resolving issues&amp;nbsp;with professionalism.&lt;br&gt;● Leadership and Development: Guide and develop Field Specialists by providing&amp;nbsp;essential tools and knowledge. Assisting with regular training sessions and ongoing&amp;nbsp;support.&lt;br&gt;● Program Optimization: Collect and analyze on-site feedback to refine program tactics,&amp;nbsp;while implementing effective solutions to boost program efficiency.&lt;br&gt;● Inventory Oversight: Aide in distribution and tracking of program materials and assets,&amp;nbsp;ensuring timely communication of issues and escalation as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years of experience in field marketing, brand activation, retail engagement, or similar roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven supervisory experience with a strong focus on team development and coaching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of compliance requirements in regulated industries and the ability to enforce guidelines consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with excellent problem-solving skills and meticulous attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to quickly learn and articulate detailed product information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with a talent for building meaningful relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be 25+ years of age with a valid driver&#39;s license and reliable transportation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-market travel required up to a 40-mile radius.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We seek a leader who thrives on being actively involved in every facet of the retail program. The&amp;nbsp;ideal candidate will be deeply involved in day-to-day operations—mentoring a team of&amp;nbsp;specialists, ensuring compliance, and driving performance across every consumer and retailer&amp;nbsp;relationship built. Your hands-on approach and commitment to excellence will directly impact&amp;nbsp;program success.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Motive is a dynamic agency and creative collective operating at the speed of culture. We’re a collective of deep thinkers, creative makers, cultural connoisseurs, and executional aces. We create meaningful engagements between brands and their audiences, cultivating relationships that drive tangible results for our clients. And we do it with sharp strategy and powerful creative executed across all the media and touch-points key to our targets’ lives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As pioneers in the area of content, digital engagement, and innovative experiential programs, and award winners for work in TV, event, digital and social, Motive has created a culture where every individual is given an opportunity to stretch and flex their creative and executional muscles daily. We are a team of hard-working, fast-moving, energetic, passionate, driven, straight-talking creative thinkers. We like being challenged and we love the collaboration necessary to overcome the challenges and succeed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If this sounds like a place you would thrive, let’s see if we can make something happen.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ASSOCIATE ACCOUNT DIRECTOR&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a hybrid position, meaning you&#39;re empowered to work from home and our local office location.&amp;nbsp; We currently require a minimum of 1 day of intentional collaboration work in the office per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At this time we are currently only interviewing candidates based in the Denver area.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Assoc. Account Director at Motive you’ll have the opportunity to manage and lead the integrated day-to-day efforts with key client relationships and accounts. You’ll partner with clients to understand their business and work with internal teams to develop meaningful fully-integrated marketing campaigns that deliver results. On any given day you will write briefs, lead creative and partnership initiatives with authority, manage and lead internal and external communications, orchestrate an organized asset delivery plan, be responsible for budgets and timelines, collaborate with creative and other internal and external teams, while managing the delivery of a variety of projects. You’ll be responsible for championing best-in-class work across traditional, social, retail, promotional, partnerships, experiential and more for some of the biggest brands in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage the day-to-day efforts with key clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and manage the the day-to-day internal project management flow for a series of high-profile projects for major international brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as key contact for projects and delivery, managing communication and asset distribution, and serving as the central touch point for questions, strategic guidance and support for client teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a variety of work streams which could include TVC, social, events, retail / shopper, POS / POP,&amp;nbsp; digital, partnerships; including creation of timelines, workflows, and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically advise clients and develop ideas and solutions that achieve business, marketing and engagement objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate client assignments into meaningful briefs for the creative teams and effectively balance dual expectations of clients and the agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a cross-studio team of art directors, copywriters, experiential leads, digital and social innovators, as well as and other client services teams to ideate and develop concepts for projects and accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-task and get the work done—on time, within project budgets and exceeding expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in big idea thinking sessions for the agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquire in-depth knowledge of, and be conversant in, client’s business, industry and competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster client relationships that run deep. Step into the role of your client&#39;s &quot;go to&quot; lead, managing proactive communications in an inspiring and professional manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively present strategic and creative platforms to internal and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 7 years of experience managing integrated (read: a combination of traditional, TVC and content, retail, shopper, digital / social partnerships and promotional) projects and accounts in a fast-paced advertising agency.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience managing several clients and projects simultaneously.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exemplary organizational skills: you&#39;re known for having your finger on the pulse and every detail locked-in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Powerhouse communications: you&#39;re clear, direct, proactive and kind. You can communicate up, down, and sideways if you have to - building trust, rapport, and relationships in the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of owned social, with experience helping shape strategies that connect brand objectives, audience behaviors and platform opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;w4vq38&quot; data-start=&quot;849&quot; data-end=&quot;996&quot;&gt;Experience with bringing content to life -&amp;nbsp;leading the development and production of still and video assets from brief through final delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with partnerships, shared IP, and creative collaborations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience crafting big idea briefs, and guiding creative concept and design work forward.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience creating and managing budgets and timelines for projects covering all of the above.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience managing team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, and a knack for delivering excellent presentations and building relationships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A strong ‘self-starter’ mentality and sense of responsibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A positive, upbeat attitude!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive is an&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;equal opportunity employer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;! We believe that a diverse team makes us stronger and smarter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive recruits, employs, trains, compensates and promotes regardless of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, veteran status, and other protected status as required by applicable law. The starting salary for this position is between $90k and $115k annually, based on experience. We offer an inspiring working environment and great benefits, including low-cost health, dental, and vision plans; unlimited flexible paid time off, 401k with annual match, an employee stock ownership program and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Motive has a clear vision: to be a creative leader where a diverse mix of talented people want to come, stay, and do their best work. We know our company succeeds only through the hard work and dedication of our passionate and creative employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Strategy &amp;amp; Activation Director, Central&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Market Strategy &amp;amp; Activation Director&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the strategy, performance, and execution of a multi-market retail engagement program within a highly regulated industry (tobacco/nicotine).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role serves as the senior leader across the field marketing organization, overseeing and developing a team of Market Managers while ensuring consistent, compliant, and high-quality execution across all markets. The ideal candidate can move seamlessly between strategy and execution, seeing the bigger picture, identifying patterns and opportunities across markets, and translating those insights into clear direction for field teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Market Strategy &amp;amp; Activation Director will be accountable for overall market performance, operational excellence, team effectiveness, and continuous program optimization. They will partner closely with agency and client stakeholders to turn program objectives into actionable market strategies, surface meaningful field intelligence, and ensure learnings from the field inform how the program evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly collaborative, hands-on leadership role for someone who understands that exceptional field marketing requires both disciplined execution and the ability to adapt quickly based on what is happening in the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Strategy &amp;amp; Program Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the overarching field strategy and activation approach across all participating markets, translating client objectives into clear priorities, expectations, and actionable plans for Market Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish consistent standards for market execution while allowing teams to respond intelligently to local market dynamics, retailer needs, consumer behavior, and emerging opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a holistic view of program performance, identifying trends, risks, opportunities, and operational needs across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with agency and client leadership to evolve program strategy based on field performance, business priorities, and marketplace learnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Manager Leadership &amp;amp; Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of Market Managers, establishing clear expectations and accountability for performance within each market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a strong operating rhythm across the field organization through regular communications, performance reviews, market check-ins, and sharing of best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Market Managers to effectively lead their local teams, solve problems, and make sound decisions while providing senior-level support and escalation when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify performance gaps and development opportunities and provide direct, actionable coaching to strengthen individual and team effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a connected field culture in which teams learn from one another rather than operating as isolated markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own overall program performance across markets, ensuring teams consistently deliver against activation schedules, retailer commitments, consumer engagement goals, reporting requirements, and other established KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish processes and standards that create consistency, accountability, and operational discipline across the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor market performance and proactively intervene when execution, staffing, inventory, retailer relationships, or other operational factors put results at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Managers and internal teams to resolve systemic challenges and eliminate recurring barriers to strong execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure program assets, inventory, staffing, and resources are effectively planned and deployed across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Program Integrity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of rigorous compliance across the field organization, ensuring Market Managers and their teams understand and consistently adhere to all regulatory, brand, retailer, and program requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear expectations and processes for monitoring compliance and reporting accuracy across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Managers to quickly address discrepancies, compliance concerns, or executional risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior escalation point for sensitive or complex field issues, partnering with agency and client leadership as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insights &amp;amp; Optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn field activity into actionable intelligence by identifying patterns across markets, consumer interactions, retailer feedback, competitive activity, and sales or performance data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look beyond individual market results to identify what is working, what is not, and where the program can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create mechanisms for sharing successful approaches and best practices across Market Managers and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate field insights into clear recommendations for agency and client stakeholders that strengthen future strategy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously challenge the program to become smarter, more efficient, and more effective over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior field marketing partner to agency and client stakeholders, providing a clear view of market performance, emerging needs, risks, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with account, strategy, operations, staffing, and other internal teams to ensure the field organization has what it needs to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a solutions-oriented perspective to program challenges, balancing client expectations, field realities, operational considerations, and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the field in broader program conversations while ensuring client and agency priorities are clearly understood and activated by market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–10+ years of experience in field marketing, experiential marketing, retail engagement, brand activation, shopper marketing, or related disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading multi-market or distributed field teams, including direct management of managers or senior field leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate broader business and marketing objectives into effective field strategies and execution plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing complex, high-volume consumer-facing programs with multiple stakeholders and operational workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of compliance requirements and operational rigor, ideally including experience within regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to analyze field performance, identify meaningful patterns, and turn insights into actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills with a track record of training, coaching, developing, and holding teams accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills with the ability to effectively engage field teams, agency leaders, clients, and retail partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and comfortable managing multiple markets, priorities, and workstreams simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and problem-solving skills, particularly in fast-moving environments where issues require timely decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel regularly to participating markets and work occasional evenings or weekends based on program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;field marketing leader who thinks like a strategist and operates like an owner&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know how to build clarity across a distributed team, empower strong managers, and create consistency without losing sight of what makes individual markets different. You are equally comfortable reviewing performance data, coaching a Market Manager, training a room full of 50 product specialists, troubleshooting an executional challenge, organizing and tracking inventory, walking a retail environment, or presenting a recommendation to senior stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most importantly, you don’t simply oversee activity—you make the entire program better. You connect dots across markets, turn field intelligence into action, anticipate what teams will need next, and create the conditions for people to deliver exceptional work consistently, responsibly, and at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Motive is a dynamic agency and creative collective operating at the speed of culture. We’re a collective of deep thinkers, creative makers, cultural connoisseurs, and executional aces. We create meaningful engagements between brands and their audiences, cultivating relationships that drive tangible results for our clients. And we do it with sharp strategy and powerful creative executed across all the media and touch-points key to our targets’ lives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As pioneers in the area of content, digital engagement, and innovative experiential programs, and award winners for work in TV, event, digital and social, Motive has created a culture where every individual is given an opportunity to stretch and flex their creative and executional muscles daily. We are a team of hard-working, fast-moving, energetic, passionate, driven, straight-talking creative thinkers. We like being challenged and we love the collaboration necessary to overcome the challenges and succeed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If this sounds like a place you would thrive, let’s see if we can make something happen.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
